# SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL — surface gap
#
# Status: parser does NOT recognise the syntax today (v7.37.8).
# Each line below is marked `statement error` so a regression is
# caught immediately when the surface lands (the assertion flips
# from "errors today" to "must accept" → the author fills in the
# behavioural checks).
#
# Per v7.38 plan §二 轴 4 + dashboard §1 metabox 4: SPG must
# accept PG-standard `SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL` and
# `START TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL`, track the current level
# per-transaction, and reflect it through
# `SHOW transaction_isolation`. The actual isolation semantics
# (REPEATABLE READ snapshot, SERIALIZABLE SSI) are separate work
# tracked in the same axis.
#
# Vision contract: SPG is to be ≥ PG on every angle
# (memory/vision-spg-ge-pg-everywhere.md). PG ships these as
# standard surface; SPG must too.
#
# When the surface lands:
# 1. Implement parser support + engine state.
# 2. Flip each `statement error` below to `statement ok`.
# 3. Add `query T nosort` blocks asserting `SHOW transaction_isolation`
#    returns the value just SET.
# 4. Update 16_isolation/_README.md status column to LANDED.

